### Health check
GET http://localhost:8080/api/health


### Get all tickets from MongoDB
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets


### Get tickets filtered by status
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets?status=OPEN


### Get tickets filtered by priority
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets?priority=HIGH


### Get tickets filtered by category
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets?category=Email


### Get paged tickets (page 0)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets/paged?page=0&size=5


### Get paged tickets (page 1)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets/paged?page=1&size=5


### Get paged tickets sorted by createdAt descending (explicit, same as default)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets/paged?page=0&size=5&sortBy=createdAt&direction=desc


### Get paged tickets sorted by title ascending
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets/paged?page=0&size=5&sortBy=title&direction=asc


### Get one ticket
# Replace the ID below with an actual ID returned by GET /api/tickets
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets/REPLACE_WITH_REAL_ID


### Get missing ticket
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets/000000000000000000000000


### Create a valid ticket
POST http://localhost:8080/api/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Cannot access email",
  "description": "User cannot login to company email account.",
  "category": "Email",
  "priority": "HIGH",
  "createdBy": "amir@example.com"
}


### Create an invalid ticket
POST http://localhost:8080/api/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "",
  "description": "",
  "category": "",
  "priority": "",
  "createdBy": ""
}
